==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Good option for beginners.
* Low cooldowns, price, and mastery requirements.
* Good for training [[Aura]] because of the low damage.
* Both moves have [[AoE]].

|'''[Z] Whirlwind'''
* Decently large hitbox.
* Decent stun.
* Low knockback, making it a reliable source of damage whilst grinding.

|'''[X] Tornado'''
* Decent [[AoE]].
* Good [[combo]] potential.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Does not [[Instinct Break|break Instinct]].
* Low damage.
* The cooldowns are very long for such a weak weapon, making it very ineffective, especially at such a low point in the game.
* For its stage in the game, the Dual Katana's upgrade cost is exorbitant due to the requirement of [[Angel Wings]], a [[Materials|Material]] that can only be dropped by enemies in [[Upper Skylands]], which are [[level]] 450+.

|'''[Z] Whirlwind'''
* Low range.
* Hard to hit in the air.

|'''[X] Tornado'''
* Limited range, making it less effective for engaging distant enemies.
* Holds the player in place.
}}
</tabber>

==Notes==
* The Dual Katana is often preferred over the [[Iron Mace]] because of its wider [[Area of Effect]] and lack of knockback on its M1s, making it more effective for grinding against multiple [[enemies]].

==Trivia==
* The Dual Katana has a higher price than two separate [[Katana]]s, despite the fact that it is comprised of only two of them.

